('What does Crimea Scout steal and when; how does Coercion value and limit a spent combat card?', 'Scout before combat randomly steals one opponent combat card to hand, once per combat not per unit. Coercion once per turn spends one combat card as any one resource regardless card value; card not worth end-game coins.',[17,21],'Distinct hand theft and resource substitution rules.'),
('How do Nordic Seaworthy and Polania Submerge differ in lake movement and retreat, and what happens to transported workers/resources when leaving a lake?', 'Both character/mechs to/from lakes, workers only via mech; cannot leave workers/resources behind when carrier leaves; worker cannot leave without mech. Nordic may retreat character/mechs onto adjacent lake (or home), carrying workers; Polania may move lake to any lake, no such special retreat. Both cannot build/deploy lake, can fight another lake-capable faction there.',[16,17],'Lake movement/retreat exceptions and mandatory cargo.'),
('When does Polania Camaraderie prevent popularity loss, and does it cover driving out undefended workers?', 'Prevents popularity loss for workers forced to retreat after winning combat as aggressor on own turn. Does not apply to driving out undefended workers without combat; normal one popularity each then.',[17,11],'Combat-only popularity exception.'),
